-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Magicland Dizzy
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1990
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy 4 - Magicland Dizzy (1990)(Code Masters)(128K).z80
  MD5         7ebfab28186697409f9026b552ccbf84

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Magicland Dizzy build moved to the 128K
              release (AY music), his plot hook at 28 MHz, whole alt ROM
              image, printer buffer put back after loading, loading screen

  Note        The 128K release, so the AY music plays. Dean Woodyatt's
              Magicland Dizzy build: Dizzy is four hardware sprites, so he no
              longer takes the colours of the scenery he walks through; his
              plot hook now runs at 28 MHz. The game's own table at 0x5B00
              (mirrored objects) is put back after loading. Loading screen
              from the tape.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Walk through walls
   3  Tune continues when dead
   4  Play at double speed
   5  Immune to flame
   6  Immune to swamp ghosts
   7  Immune to rat
   8  Immune to bats

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

