-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      NOT IDENTICAL (PARTIAL): 3 bot walks of the 128K release (12,013
              / 12,028 / 12,020 frames) on rework v128: every hook event
              identical to the original (4,684 plots, 4,695 erases, 21,245 ISR
              hide checks, 135 room wipes, 47 inventory boxes), 4,713 sprite
              plots pixel-perfect; but 5 of 101,594 pixel tests read a byte
              where the original's own erase had left a hole (another routine
              drew over Dizzy before his XOR erase): the build keeps that
              background pixel, so those 5 tests differ from the original
              (Dean's 48K build has the same property, the same code);
              negatives: 6 broken builds, 5 caught by their own signal, the
              wipe hide alone masked by the ISR hide; clock matrix 5 hook
              sites x 4 incoming clocks = 20 cases PASS, a forced 3.5 MHz exit
              detected; ROM paths: every ROM byte as recorded; start-up tail
              never read before written; printer buffer as the snapshot after
              NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: loading screen, title, play reached,
              frames viewed; AY music written (750 data writes a second in
              play, as the original); flicker 300 frames: 0 out of step, 0
              vanished, 0 transients; 15-minute soak against the original
              .z80: no freeze, loop or crash, AY 737 writes a second in both;
              no person played it

  Coverage    the first rooms only (bot walks: Weirdhenge, the Mysterious
              Monolith, Bushy Grove, the Haunted Swamp, Down a Well), the
              inventory box, deaths and game over; loading screen stub in bank
              13, emulator-tested only; cheats proved in the simulator on the
              original 128K file: Infinite Lives (a death: lives 3 -> 3
              against 3 -> 2), Walk through walls (holding left: 4 rooms and
              90 positions against 1 room and 12; holding right he passes the
              rock at the swamp's edge that stops him without it), Tune
              continues when dead (4,500 AY writes in the 300 frames after a
              death against 540), Play at double speed (185 player updates in
              1,000 frames against 127), Immune to Flame / Swamp Ghosts / Rat
              / Bats (each hazard's damage call run from a play state: energy
              31 -> 31 against 30 / 27 / 28 / 30; flame and swamp ghost hits
              also met on the bot walks); none dropped

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
